  "reconsidered_answer": "Your plan to listen to Jonah's revised cut before deciding on postponement is an excellent, practical step. By putting the edit first, you move the conversation away from abstract arguments and ground it in concrete creative choices. Comparing his revisions directly to the cut approved three months ago and documenting the precise interpretive differences will help you clarify what remains a fundamental concern of representational integrity versus what is a difference in artistic taste.

Regarding the credit dispute, your proposal of an equal top-line credit combined with detailed role descriptions below is a balanced compromise. It respects Jonah's fear of splitting the work into a false art-versus-journalism dichotomy while preserving the specificity of your actual labor (reporting and interviewing versus sound and structure). However, as you noted, credit cannot retroactively repair the informal, mismatched decision-making process of the last eighteen months. 

